                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 24.</note>
                <note rend="inline" type="source"><hi rendition="#small-caps">No. 153.]</hi></note>
                <head>Mr. Davis to Mr. E. B.
                        Washburne.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-08-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 16, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatches, numbered 232 to 242, both inclusive.</p>
                <p>Your action in regard to the protection of subjects of Saxony and of those of the
                    Grand Duke of Hesse, in France, as indicated in your Nos. 234 and 235, is fully
                    approved.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. C. B. DAVIS, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
